---
permalink: /search.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  The search index, one record per SECTION of a page rather than one per page.

  Two problems this fixes.

  1. Text was fused together. The old index did `strip_html | strip_newlines`,
     and stripping tags from `<p>a</p><p>b</p>` yields "ab" — no separator —
     while strip_newlines removed the only thing keeping blocks apart. That
     produced "healthcheckcd" and "hash.pyp" in the index, which broke snippets
     AND matching: "healthcheck" and "cd" no longer existed as separate words.
     Inserting a space before every tag before stripping is the whole fix.

  2. A result pointed at a page. On a long runbook that is a weak answer, so
     each `<h2>`/`<h3>` now gets its own record with its own anchor. Clicking a
     result lands on the heading, not the top of the document.

  A page-level record is emitted too, so searching a page by name still finds
  the page itself — search.js ranks those above heading records.

  Fields: t title · h heading ("" on page records) · u url · c category
          s section · b badge · x text
{%- endcomment -%}
[
  {%- assign first = true -%}
  {%- for meta in site.data.sections -%}
    {%- include nav-docs.html key=meta.key -%}
    {%- for doc in nav_docs -%}
      {%- include doc-title.html doc=doc -%}
      {%- assign d_cat = doc.category | default: meta.label -%}
      {%- assign d_badge = meta.badge | default: meta.label | slice: 0, 1 -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        A page may opt out of content indexing with `search_content: false`.
        It still gets one record so it can be found by name; only its body and
        headings are left out.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if doc.search_content == false -%}
        {%- unless first %},{% endunless -%}{%- assign first = false -%}
  {
    "t": {{ doc_title | jsonify }},
    "h": "",
    "u": {{ doc.url | jsonify }},
    "c": {{ d_cat | jsonify }},
    "s": {{ meta.label | jsonify }},
    "b": {{ d_badge | jsonify }},
    "x": {{ doc.description | default: "" | jsonify }}
  }
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Split on headings; the first chunk is the page intro. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign chunks = doc.content | split: "<h" -%}

      {%- for chunk in chunks -%}
        {%- assign emit = false -%}
        {%- assign h_title = "" -%}
        {%- assign h_url = doc.url -%}
        {%- assign raw = "" -%}

        {%- if forloop.first -%}
          {%- comment -%} intro: everything before the first heading {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign raw = chunk -%}
          {%- assign emit = true -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign hparts = chunk | split: "</h" -%}
          {%- assign hhead = hparts | first -%}
          {%- assign hlevel = hhead | slice: 0, 1 -%}
          {%- if hlevel == "2" or hlevel == "3" -%}
            {%- assign h_title = hhead | split: ">" | last | strip_html | strip -%}
            {%- if hhead contains 'id="' -%}
              {%- assign h_id = hhead | split: 'id="' | last | split: '"' | first -%}
              {%- assign h_url = doc.url | append: "#" | append: h_id -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign raw = chunk | remove_first: hhead | remove_first: "</h" | remove_first: hlevel | remove_first: ">" -%}
            {%- assign emit = true -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if emit -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The space before "<" is what stops adjacent blocks welding
            together; normalize_whitespace then collapses the runs.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            doc.content is the page BEFORE wikilinks.html runs, so [[links]]
            are still raw here, and strip_html leaves entities encoded. Both
            leaked into snippets as "[[Docker Swarm]]" and "ssh.&lt;ID&gt;".
            Brackets go; entities are decoded back to the characters a reader
            typed, which is also what they will search for.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign text = raw | replace: "<", " <" | strip_html -%}
          {%- assign text = text | replace: "[[", "" | replace: "]]", "" -%}
          {%- assign text = text | replace: "&lt;", "<" | replace: "&gt;", ">" -%}
          {%- assign text = text | replace: "&quot;", '"' | replace: "&#39;", "'" -%}
          {%- assign text = text | replace: "&amp;", "&" -%}
          {%- assign text = text | normalize_whitespace | strip -%}
          {%- if text != "" or h_title != "" -%}
            {%- unless first %},{% endunless -%}{%- assign first = false -%}
  {
    "t": {{ doc_title | jsonify }},
    "h": {{ h_title | jsonify }},
    "u": {{ h_url | jsonify }},
    "c": {{ d_cat | jsonify }},
    "s": {{ meta.label | jsonify }},
    "b": {{ d_badge | jsonify }},
    "x": {{ text | truncate: 1200, "" | jsonify }}
  }
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
]
